	order_index: 1
	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"&oHi!&r Welcome to &lThe Gardener Was Replaced&r, a pack which (as you could've guessed) was heavily inspired by &lThe Farmer Was Replaced&r, a game you should go play if you haven't yet (of course, only after playing this pack)."
				""
				"&lThis pack&r will take you through the basics of the &oLua programming language&r as you will be controlling the bot &o(nicknamed turtle due to programmer reasons)&r you can see on your screen right now through it."
				""
				"&lTo begin&r, first press the checkmark to complete this quest. This will allow you to get upgrades required to progress through the gameplay."
				""
				"&lThen, press the &oE key&r. You will notice that your inventory has been replaced with a terminal. This will be your gateway to run code on the farming bot to make it actually do things."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&lIf you are not familiar with how the terminal works&r, don't worry. All you will need is a couple of basic commands:"
				""
				"&lFirstly&r, and most importantly, the &6edit <filename>&r command will allow you to edit a file with the specified filename. Once you run it, the text editing environment should be easy enough to understand. Press &oCTRL&r to save the file and exit the editor."
				""
				"&lNext&r, to actually run your script type in the &6filename&r you gave it. The file must have the suffix &o.lua&r, but you don't need to specify it to run. &lIf you created a file without a suffix&r, it will be .lua by default. You can have multiple scripts on your turtle at the same time."
				""
				"&lLastly&r, if you want to quickly run some lua code without creating a script, you can use the &oREPL&r by running the &6lua&r command. &lIt is not recommended&r to run &oall&r of your code that way."
				""
				"&lThat's not all&r of the existing command. You might also wanna list files with &6ls&r or remove them using &6rm&r, but that's mostly all that you will need. &lFor everything else&r, don't be afraid to search it up on the web!"
				""
				"&lThis modpack uses&r a popular mod by the name of &oCC: Tweaked&r to do all of the programming related things, so look up a few tutorials for it if you don't yet feel comfortable using it!"
				""
				"&oNow,&r let's actually do something with your little &lrobo-friend&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
			]
			disable_toast: true
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "computercraft:turtle_normal"
				tag: {
					RightUpgrade: "minecraft:diamond_hoe"
					RightUpgradeNbt: {
						Tag: {
							Damage: 0
						}
					}
				}
			}
			id: "43D29D4E29B39AF3"
			shape: "rsquare"
			size: 2.0d
			subtitle: "And it begins..."
			tasks: [{
				id: "0C7B73BF7352C3D0"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Start Here!"
			x: 1.0d
			y: -6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["43D29D4E29B39AF3"]
			description: [
				"&lThe gameplay loop&r of this pack will consist of you completing various tasks &o(usually related to gathering some flowers)&r in exchange for unlocking new mechanics."
				""
				"&lYour first task&r is to simply move the turtle. For that, you will first need to &oimport&r the tools used for controlling it. For that, simply add this line to your script:"
				""
				"&7turtle = &6require&7(&b\"turtle\"&7)&r"
				""
				"&lYou are now able&r to access various commands in code that are related to controlling the turtle, specifically:"
				""
				"&7turtle.&6forward&7()&r"
				"&7turtle.&6back&7()&r"
				"&7turtle.&6turnLeft&7()&r"
				"&7turtle.&6turnRight&7()&r"
				""
				"&lAll of which&r do exactly what you think &othey would do.&r Try out some of them to unlock your first plant - the &l&eYellow Mystical Flower&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&lTo plant said flower&r, you will need to import a list of all plants. &oThat&r can be located within the \"&oconsts&r\" package."
				""
				"&lLet's import that&r similar to how we imported the instructions for the turtle:"
				""
				"&7consts = &6require&7(&b\"consts\"&7)&r"
				""
				"&lNow we can access&r what's called an \"&oenum&r\" of all possible by using:"
				""
				"&7consts.&6PLANTS&7.&6YELLOW_FLOWER&r"
				""
				"&lIf you have never coded before&r, just think of it as a list, with each plant having a name attached to it, all in UPPERCASE replacing spaces with underscores &o(as per programmer tradition)&r. Now the value is not useful by itself, we're only basically telling the computer to think of it."
				""
				"&lTo actually do something with it&r, we need to pass it to another turtle instruction as an \"&oargument&r\", telling the turtle to actually place it:"
				""
				"&7turtle.&6plant&7(consts.&6PLANTS&7.&6YELLOW_FLOWER&7)&r"
				""
				"&lCongrats!&r You have now officially planted your first flower. It will take a bit to grow, but when it does you can use another command to gather its &opetals&r (the turtle must be right above it):"
				""
				"&7turtle.&6gather&7()&r"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&lTo maximize efficiency&r, you might want to use all of the space proived to you to grow flowers &oin parallel.&r For that, move your turtle around and plant the flowers accordingly using the previously supplied commands."
				""
				"&lLua also provides&r a couple options for loops, specifically &9while&r and &9for&r, as well as an &9if&r conditional statement. If you are a programmer you already know what they do, otherwise feel free to research them in order to optimize the space your code takes up."
				""
				"&lWhile your turtle&r is moving around, it might be important to gather some data about the world surrounding it, you can do that by calling the following turtle instructions and writing them to \"&ovariables&r\" - boxes of data that you can use later in your code:"
				""
				"&7x, y = turtle.&6getCoords&7()&r"
				"&7facing = turtle.&6getFacing&7()&r"
				"&7grown = turtle.&6getGrown&7()&r"
				"&7plant = turtle.&6getPlant&7()&r"
				""
				"&lThese&r return the coordinates of the turtle, the way its facing (east, west, north, or south respectfully), whether the plant beneath the turtle has grown yet, and the name of the plant below the turtle respectfully."
				""
				"&lNote&r that &6getFacing&r and &6getPlant&r return \"&ostrings&r\" - lines of text; &6getGrown&r returns a \"&oboolean&r\" - true or false value; and &6getCoords&r returns two numbers - &ox&r and &oy&r respectfully."
				""
				"&lYou can rename these&r variables however you want and access them by said names."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&lP.S:&r if you need more info about any of the concepts listed here or later, check out the documentation chapter of this guidebook."
				""
				"&lAccessing external resources&r on the internet might be useful as well."
			]
			disable_toast: true
			icon: "botania:yellow_mystical_flower"
			id: "7A4D621495E38EB4"
